#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:55
#: 9784e6c67f7d4946b3cf2da88fe3f5f7
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:57
#: 70a8c3b0ab6145b9bd0d5c0170f1fb1a
msgid "RC input is configured by default via the USART2 RX input. It supports all serial RC protocols except PPM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:59
#: 88ae2cf6655d41e0ac9e86f93efb9d81
msgid "Note: If the receiver is FPort the receiver must be tied to the USART2 TX pin , RSSI_TYPE set to 3, and SERIAL2_OPTIONS must be set to 7 (invert TX/RX, half duplex). For full duplex like CRSF/ELRS use both RX1 and TX1 and set RSSI_TYPE also to 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:64
#: 22fb198e5e9a4c3f8ec49d58408d85dc
msgid "FrSky Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:66
#: 496982f1a72c497880e4d08aae979c96
msgid "FrSky Telemetry is supported using an unused UART, such as the T3 pin (UART3 transmit). You need to set the following parameters to enable support for FrSky S.PORT:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:70
#: 3375f177bbc94ae980dcc8c6c7e658a7
msgid "SERIAL3_PROTOCOL 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:71
#: 833431817b454e6084950cf32183c27c
msgid "SERIAL3_OPTIONS 7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:74
#: 63fbe200f3db44b8a43f2be9f7c4653a
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:76
#: b559bd89ea7a45f9a6bf6337a36d530d
msgid "The Flywoo H743 Pro supports OSD using OSD_TYPE 1 (MAX7456 driver) and simultaneously DisplayPort using TX8/RX8 on the HD VTX connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:79
#: e5cf55dbdae148dcbdd470878a78fbaa
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:81
#: 5cf78091b1514176813a4996bf72e24d
msgid "The Flywoo H743 Pro supports up to 13 PWM or DShot outputs. The pads for motor output M1 to M8 are provided on both the motor connectors and on separate pads, plus M9-13 on a separate pads for LED strip and other PWM outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:85
#: 29eaf67324ca4b19aa6acf17e7b937d1
msgid "The PWM is in 4 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:88
#: 32de27689b964f61b0d0c0adba09352f
msgid "PWM 1-2   in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:89
#: 6994367ffa844b7895188c6c1f88f9e9
msgid "PWM 3-6   in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:90
#: 0dfd67a644f845038c700f6ce50a8a8c
msgid "PWM 7-10  in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:91
#: 4987d4a03c734f13851c16477d97c7cc
msgid "PWM 11-12 in group4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:92
#: ce4d519e69154faab9066c39e5db46c0
msgid "PWM 13    in group5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:94
#: 61e17542231f476497c9d983b0cbbe33
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot. Channels 1-10 support bi-directional dshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:99
#: ae154f9c2c4345b1a410eba25b2e4c4e
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:101
#: 9ea8f51444234568b824207afc2eb014
msgid "The board has a built-in voltage sensor and external current sensor input. The current sensor can read up to 130 Amps. The voltage sensor can handle up to 6S LiPo batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:105
#: d407e814fecd4f9cba911f983dabdf6a
msgid "The correct battery setting parameters are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:108
#: 42e245fd919243f782cbdf9ec0498ebe
msgid "BATT_MONITOR 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:109
#: f70d275a3d484973816956bf1e0ca9ca
msgid "BATT_VOLT_PIN 11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:110
#: 66ebd0195a0e46c1b8d66e1f69f30fc2
msgid "BATT_CURR_PIN 13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:111
#: 9c313c95d45d4b63b8b2f808840f4156
msgid "BATT_VOLT_MULT 11.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:112
#: db77e8be7174487a8a5ce0624e36fdec
msgid "BATT_AMP_PERVLT 40"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:115
#: 6e7cfb6e2033482a9e9017e9efb5b45e
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:117
#: 70aaf71972c242ffbaa1678afaa7f2ef
msgid "The Flywoo H743 Pro does not have a builtin compass, but you can attach an external compass using I2C on the SDA and SCL pads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:120
#: d0130ab7aea14995a42f4134c0b41bc1
msgid "VTX power control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:122
#: 030f7eb84edf4c74a44a552579d9c432
msgid "GPIO 81 controls the VTX BEC output to pins marked \"10V\". Setting this GPIO low removes voltage supply to pins. By default RELAY2 is configured to control this pin and sets the GPIO high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:126
#: 6f1fde8b6a4a452d8266b8c96a236dc1
msgid "Camera control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:128
#: 19cb92bd74a64528b75c00956040b054
msgid "GPIO 82 controls the camera output to the connectors marked \"CAM1\" and \"CAM2\". Setting this GPIO low switches the video output from CAM1 to CAM2. By default RELAY3 is configured to control this pin and sets the GPIO high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:131
#: 24073c355c7e48399190aa326999665b
msgid "Loading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:133
#: ad982b843b00400c8dcb1f49255c3c35
msgid "Initial firmware load can be done with DFU by plugging in USB with the bootloader button pressed. Then you should load the \"with_bl.hex\" firmware, using your favourite DFU loading tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-flywoo-h743.rst:137
#: ede03f6fe06141fd856c6d83c61eafb9
msgid "Once the initial firmware is loaded you can update the firmware using any ArduPilot ground station software. Updates should be done with the \\*.apj firmware files."
msgstr ""
